<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>For the love of Christ constrains,</l><l>As a narrow road with walls;</l><l>In this way we are compelled</l><l>By Christ’s love to live to Him.</l><l>For the love of Christ constrains,</l><l>One died on behalf of all,</l><l>So conclude that all have died.</l><l>To ourselves we may not live.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>For the love of Christ constrains</l><l>Us to live not to ourselves,</l><l>But to Him who died for us,</l><l>Who for us has now been raised.</l><l>For the love of Christ constrains</l><l>By the loving death of Christ,</l><l>That we, motivated thus,</l><l>Live a loving life for Him.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>For the love of Christ constrains,</l><l>Or we would not live to Him,</l><l>Nor from old life would refrain,</l><l>But His love does press us in.</l><l>For the love of Christ constrains,</l><l>Causes us our life to lose.</l><l>Lord, we’re captive in Your love,</l><l>Willingly we live to You.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
